# DRIFT VICTORY
# THIS COPY HAS A LEAD MELODY ON CHANNEL 3, WRITTEN BY CLAUDE AS AN EXAMPLE of what could go
# there. It is not Greg's writing. The accompaniment is the same as in songs/drift/.
# A small win: a relaxed jingle, IV - V - I, chip chords and a last hit. Plays once.
# DRIFT, a chill suite for one game: TITLE, CAFE, FIELD, RAIN, NIGHT, VICTORY, GAME OVER and
# CREDITS. All in B flat major or its relative G minor, laid-back, on one set of
# instruments. The title is New song's Chill style with its defaults, in B flat.
#
# A starting point made by PokeyTracker's New song window, by rule: each section's beat, bass
# and accompaniment worked out from the key, the chords and the band chosen. The tune is yours.
# Chords: IV V I I:  Eb F Bb Bb.
# The format is in Demo1/CLAUDE.md, under "Song files".

song   DRIFT VICTORY
key    B FLAT MAJOR

# Distortion C, for a bass. Its table skips notes - see which in the tracker's colours.
instrument BASS
  table      buzz
  volume     12 11 10 9 8
  distortion buzz
  release    3

# A plain square wave, for a tune.
instrument LEAD
  table      tone
  volume     12 11 10 10 9
  distortion tone
  release    2

# Soft keys for an accompaniment: struck, then falling away.
instrument KEYS
  table      tone
  volume     11 10 9 8 8 7 7 6 6 5 5 4
  distortion tone
  release    3

# Four drums: a falling thump, a burst of noise, and a short and a long hiss. Each is a
# table of registers a frame at a time, with no note table, so a key only says which drum.
instrument KICK
  table      none
  volume     15 13 10 7 4 2 0
  distortion buzz
  audf       40 55 70 85 100 115 130

instrument SNARE
  table      none
  volume     13 11 9 7 5 4 3 2 1 0
  distortion tone noise
  audf       50 8 9 10 11 12 13

instrument HAT
  table      none
  volume     8 5 3 1 0
  distortion noise
  audf       2

instrument OPEN
  table      none
  volume     8 7 6 5 4 3 2 2 1 1 0
  distortion noise
  audf       1

channel 1 drums DRUMS
  kit   K=KICK S=SNARE H=HAT O=OPEN
  track INTRO K . H .  H . H .  S . H .  H . H .
  track INTRO2 K . H .  S . H .  K . S .  S S S S
  track END    O . . .  . . . .  . . . .  . . . .

channel 2 notes BASS
  note  Bass: root and fifth, on the chords' roots.
  voice BASS
  track INTRO Eb1 . . .  . . . .  Bb1 . . .  . . . .
  track INTRO2 F1 . . .  . . . .  C1 . . .  . . . .
  track END    Bb1 . . .  . . . .  . . . .  . . . .

channel 3 notes LEAD
  note  An example lead melody, written by Claude - not Greg's. The tracks are named M + the section's chord track.
  voice LEAD
  track MINTRO Bb4 . Bb4 .  Bb4 . . .  G4 . Bb4 .  Eb5 . . .
  track MINTRO2 C5 . C5 .  C5 . . .  A4 . C5 .  F5 . . .
  track MEND    D5 . . .  F5 . . .  . . . .  - . . .

channel 4 notes CHORDS
  note  The chords, in each section's own rhythm.
  voice KEYS
  track INTRO Eb . . .  Eb . . .  Eb . . .  Eb . . .
  track INTRO2 F . . .  F . . .  F . . .  F . . .
  track END    Bb . . .  . . . .  . . . .  . . . .

# The order list: a section at a time.
speed  7
section INTRO
line   INTRO  INTRO  MINTRO  INTRO
line   INTRO2  INTRO2  MINTRO2  INTRO2
section END
line   END  END  MEND  END
end
